Ballot Issue 4C

For the purpose of making additional General Fund revenue available for the purposes described below, shall taxes be increased for Arapahoe County School District Number Six (Littleton Public Schools) by $12,000,000 in 2020 for collection in 2021 and by whatever amounts are raised each year thereafter through an increased mill levy, provided that the mill levy for the first year shall not exceed 6 mills and that no year-to-year increase in the mill levy thereafter shall exceed 1 mill in any given year, and further that said mill levy may be increased annually so that the amount of revenue produced by said mill levy reflects the percentage increase in inflation, with the effect that more General Fund revenue will be available for purposes such as:
continuing to attract and retain quality teachers;
maintaining school counseling for mental health and suicide prevention;
providing classes in career orientation, technology, and specialized trades that offer students real-world job skills, such as health care, specialized trades, and computer sciences;

Shall those additional revenues from this tax increase, applied in accordance with Section 22-54-108.7, C.R.S., be deposited in the Supplemental Capital Construction, Technology, and Maintenance Fund and be used for ongoing cash funding for capital construction, new educational technology, modernization of existing technologies, and the district's maintenance needs?;

And shall the district be authorized to increase said mill levy beginning with tax collections for the year 2022 and annually thereafter in order to offset property tax refunds or mitigations or reductions in the percentage of actual valuation used to determine valuation?
